@host = http://localhost:5187

# Story 06 - multi-department and multi-branch organisation scoping. Run against a Development API
# (`docker compose up -d` first, then `dotnet run --project backend/src/Crm.Api --launch-profile http`).
# X-Dev-User is honoured in Development only (Story 07 deletes it and issues real JWTs instead).
# Well-known dev-seed ids (Crm.Modules.Organisation.Contracts.DevSeed.OrganisationDevSeed):
@admin = 06000000-0000-0000-0003-000000000001
@supervisor = 06000000-0000-0000-0003-000000000002
@agentA = 06000000-0000-0000-0003-000000000003
@agentB = 06000000-0000-0000-0003-000000000004
@ryCare = 06000000-0000-0000-0002-000000000001
@ryBill = 06000000-0000-0000-0002-000000000002
@jeCare = 06000000-0000-0000-0002-000000000003
@supervisorBillingMembershipId = 06000000-0000-0000-0004-000000000005

### 1. GET MyScope as admin - 200, three departments, roles ["Administrator"]
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/MyScope
X-Dev-User: {{admin}}

### 2. Same, Accept-Language: ar - names unchanged (both languages are always returned)
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/MyScope
X-Dev-User: {{admin}}
Accept-Language: ar

### 3. As supervisor - two departments with roles Supervisor/Agent (R4, R5: two departments on the FIRST call
### after startup; the log shows GetMembershipsOfUserQuery handled before GetMyScopeQuery)
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/MyScope
X-Dev-User: {{supervisor}}

### 4. As supervisor + X-Crm-Scope: ryBill - activeDepartmentId = ryBill
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/MyScope
X-Dev-User: {{supervisor}}
X-Crm-Scope: {{ryBill}}

### 5. As agentA + X-Crm-Scope: jeCare (a department agentA does not belong to) - 403
### urn:crm:problem:forbidden, code Organisation.ActiveScopeRejected (forged header AC), Warning log line
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/MyScope
X-Dev-User: {{agentA}}
X-Crm-Scope: {{jeCare}}

### 6. As agentA + X-Crm-Scope: not-a-guid - 403, same code
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/MyScope
X-Dev-User: {{agentA}}
X-Crm-Scope: not-a-guid

### 7. No X-Dev-User, GET MyScope - 401 problem
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/MyScope

### 8. No X-Dev-User, GET Admin/Branches - 401 (R6: [Authorize] enforced with no explicit UseRouting())
GET {{host}}/api/Admin/Branches

### 9. As agentA (not an Administrator), GET Admin/Branches - 403 (R6)
GET {{host}}/api/Admin/Branches
X-Dev-User: {{agentA}}

### 10a. As admin: GET Admin/Branches - 2 rows (Riyadh, Jeddah)
GET {{host}}/api/Admin/Branches
X-Dev-User: {{admin}}

### 10b. Create a branch - 200, code DMM
# @name createdBranch
POST {{host}}/api/Admin/Branches
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-User: {{admin}}

{ "code": "dmm", "nameAr": "الدمام", "nameEn": "Dammam" }

@branchId = {{createdBranch.response.body.id}}
@branchRowVersion = {{createdBranch.response.body.rowVersion}}

### 10c. Repeat with the same code - 409 Organisation.BranchCodeTaken
POST {{host}}/api/Admin/Branches
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-User: {{admin}}

{ "code": "dmm", "nameAr": "x", "nameEn": "y" }

### 10d. Rename it - 200
# @name renamedBranch
PUT {{host}}/api/Admin/Branches/{{branchId}}/name
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-User: {{admin}}

{ "nameAr": "الدمام الكبرى", "nameEn": "Greater Dammam", "rowVersion": "{{branchRowVersion}}" }

@branchRowVersion2 = {{renamedBranch.response.body.rowVersion}}

### 10e. Deactivate it - 200, isActive: false
# @name deactivatedBranch
POST {{host}}/api/Admin/Branches/{{branchId}}/deactivate
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-User: {{admin}}

{ "rowVersion": "{{branchRowVersion2}}" }

@branchRowVersion3 = {{deactivatedBranch.response.body.rowVersion}}

### 10f. Deactivate again - 422 Organisation.BranchAlreadyInactive
POST {{host}}/api/Admin/Branches/{{branchId}}/deactivate
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-User: {{admin}}

{ "rowVersion": "{{branchRowVersion3}}" }

### 10g. GET ?activeOnly=true - Dammam absent
GET {{host}}/api/Admin/Branches?activeOnly=true
X-Dev-User: {{admin}}

### 10h. GET (no filter) - Dammam present
GET {{host}}/api/Admin/Branches
X-Dev-User: {{admin}}

### 11a. Create a department on the deactivated Dammam branch - 422 Organisation.BranchInactive
POST {{host}}/api/Admin/Departments
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-User: {{admin}}

{ "branchId": "{{branchId}}", "code": "DMM-CARE", "nameAr": "خدمة العملاء", "nameEn": "Customer Care" }

### 11b. Create a department on Riyadh (active) - 200
# @name createdDepartment
POST {{host}}/api/Admin/Departments
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-User: {{admin}}

{ "branchId": "06000000-0000-0000-0001-000000000001", "code": "RYD-TEST", "nameAr": "قسم تجريبي", "nameEn": "Test Department" }

@departmentId = {{createdDepartment.response.body.id}}
@departmentRowVersion = {{createdDepartment.response.body.rowVersion}}

### 11c. Rename it - 200
# @name renamedDepartment
PUT {{host}}/api/Admin/Departments/{{departmentId}}/name
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-User: {{admin}}

{ "nameAr": "قسم تجريبي 2", "nameEn": "Test Department 2", "rowVersion": "{{departmentRowVersion}}" }

@departmentRowVersion2 = {{renamedDepartment.response.body.rowVersion}}

### 11d. Deactivate it - 200
POST {{host}}/api/Admin/Departments/{{departmentId}}/deactivate
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-User: {{admin}}

{ "rowVersion": "{{departmentRowVersion2}}" }

### 11e. GET ?activeOnly=true - hides it
GET {{host}}/api/Admin/Departments?activeOnly=true
X-Dev-User: {{admin}}

### 12. Validation: empty code/names + Accept-Language: ar - 400 with Arabic messages for Code, NameAr, NameEn
POST {{host}}/api/Admin/Branches
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: ar
X-Dev-User: {{admin}}

{ "code": "x", "nameAr": "", "nameEn": "" }

### 13a. Memberships as admin: GET ?userId=supervisor - 2 rows
# @name supervisorMemberships
GET {{host}}/api/Admin/Memberships?userId={{supervisor}}
X-Dev-User: {{admin}}

### 13b. Duplicate membership {supervisor, ryCare, Agent} - 409 Organisation.MembershipExists
POST {{host}}/api/Admin/Memberships
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-User: {{admin}}

{ "userId": "{{supervisor}}", "departmentId": "{{ryCare}}", "role": "Agent" }

### 13c. Change the supervisor's ryBill membership role - 200. RowVersion comes from request 13a's list
### (JSONPath: the row whose departmentId is ryBill) - never guessed, always the last-seen value.
PUT {{host}}/api/Admin/Memberships/{{supervisorBillingMembershipId}}/role
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-User: {{admin}}

{ "role": "Supervisor", "rowVersion": "{{supervisorMemberships.response.body.$[?(@.departmentId=='06000000-0000-0000-0002-000000000002')].rowVersion}}" }

### 14. CROSS-DEPARTMENT MATRIX SETUP - as agentA, create a sample with no departmentId (resolves to ryCare,
### agentA's single department) - 200
# @name sampleA
POST {{host}}/api/Admin/Samples
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-User: {{agentA}}

{ "name": "A only", "lines": [] }

@sampleAId = {{sampleA.response.body.id}}
@sampleARowVersion = {{sampleA.response.body.rowVersion}}

### 15. As agentB, create with departmentId: ryCare (a foreign department) - 403 Organisation.OutOfScope
### (write into a foreign department)
POST {{host}}/api/Admin/Samples
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-User: {{agentB}}

{ "name": "B into A", "lines": [], "departmentId": "{{ryCare}}" }

### 16. As agentB, GET sampleA - 403 Organisation.OutOfScope (read)
GET {{host}}/api/Admin/Samples/{{sampleAId}}
X-Dev-User: {{agentB}}

### 17. As agentB, PUT sampleA - 403 (update)
PUT {{host}}/api/Admin/Samples/{{sampleAId}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-User: {{agentB}}

{ "name": "hijacked", "rowVersion": "{{sampleARowVersion}}" }

### 18. As agentB, DELETE sampleA - 403 (delete)
DELETE {{host}}/api/Admin/Samples/{{sampleAId}}
X-Dev-User: {{agentB}}

### 19. As agentA, GET a random id - 404 (a real miss stays 404, never confused with the 403 above)
GET {{host}}/api/Admin/Samples/00000000-0000-0000-0000-00000000dead
X-Dev-User: {{agentA}}

### 20. As agentA, GET Admin/Samples (THE NAIVE QUERY, no scope criteria in the spec) - contains "A only",
### nothing from Jeddah. Read the EF log: WHERE has [s].[IsDeleted] = CAST(0 AS bit),
### [s].[TenantId] = @..., [s].[BranchId] = @... (or IN (...) with >1 branch), [s].[DepartmentId] = @... (or
### IN (...) with >1 department) - naive-query AC; proves R1-R3.
GET {{host}}/api/Admin/Samples
X-Dev-User: {{agentA}}

### 21. As agentB, GET Admin/Samples - does not contain "A only" (R2: same process, different rows per user)
GET {{host}}/api/Admin/Samples
X-Dev-User: {{agentB}}

### 22a. As supervisor, create one sample with X-Crm-Scope: ryBill (lands in ryBill)
POST {{host}}/api/Admin/Samples
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-User: {{supervisor}}
X-Crm-Scope: {{ryBill}}

{ "name": "billing sample", "lines": [] }

### 22b. As supervisor, GET Admin/Samples with no header - union: "A only" AND the billing one
GET {{host}}/api/Admin/Samples
X-Dev-User: {{supervisor}}

### 22c. As supervisor + X-Crm-Scope: ryCare - only ryCare rows ("A only", not the billing one)
GET {{host}}/api/Admin/Samples
X-Dev-User: {{supervisor}}
X-Crm-Scope: {{ryCare}}

### 22d. As supervisor + X-Crm-Scope: ryBill - only the billing row
GET {{host}}/api/Admin/Samples
X-Dev-User: {{supervisor}}
X-Crm-Scope: {{ryBill}}

### 23. As supervisor with no header (two departments, ambiguous), POST without departmentId - 400
### Organisation.DepartmentRequired (ambiguous target)
POST {{host}}/api/Admin/Samples
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-User: {{supervisor}}

{ "name": "ambiguous", "lines": [] }

### 24a. SOFT-DELETED ROWS STAY HIDDEN WHEN SCOPE IS LIFTED - as admin, remove the supervisor's ryBill
### membership - 204
DELETE {{host}}/api/Admin/Memberships/{{supervisorBillingMembershipId}}
X-Dev-User: {{admin}}

### 24b. Request 3 again (as supervisor) - only ryCare now. The EF log of the sign-in lookup
### (MembershipsOfUserSpecification) shows [m].[IsDeleted] = CAST(0 AS bit) and NO TenantId predicate
### (the scope filter is fully lifted; the soft-delete filter is not)
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/MyScope
X-Dev-User: {{supervisor}}

### 24c. Restore it - POST Admin/Memberships {supervisor, ryBill, Agent} (the filtered unique index allows a
### fresh row even though the old, soft-deleted one still holds that (user, department) pair)
POST {{host}}/api/Admin/Memberships
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-User: {{admin}}

{ "userId": "{{supervisor}}", "departmentId": "{{ryBill}}", "role": "Agent" }
